# The demo's front end, standing in for a login: where a real deployment's
# proxy signs a viewer in with an identity provider and tells perdu their
# groups and name, this one lets them pick one of three logins on /login,
# remembers it in a cookie of its own, and turns it into the identity
# headers perdu reads, Remote-Groups and Remote-Name. /logout forgets it,
# and a request with no login is sent to /login.
{
	admin off
}

:80 {
	# Each login's groups and name, by the cookie.
	map {cookie.demo_login} {demo_groups} {demo_name} {
		guest guest ""
		user users Sam
		admin users,admins Alex
	}

	handle /login {
		root * /srv
		rewrite * /login.html
		file_server
	}

	@login {
		method POST
		path_regexp login ^/login/(guest|user|admin)$
	}
	handle @login {
		header Set-Cookie "demo_login={re.login.1}; Path=/; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax"
		redir * / 303
	}

	handle /logout {
		header Set-Cookie "demo_login=; Path=/; Max-Age=0; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax"
		redir * /login 303
	}

	handle {
		@anonymous not vars {cookie.demo_login} guest user admin
		redir @anonymous /login 303

		# Replacing whatever the browser sends, so that a viewer can't
		# name groups of their own.
		reverse_proxy perdu:8080 {
			header_up Remote-Groups {demo_groups}
			header_up Remote-Name {demo_name}
		}
	}
}
